      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A young farmer was disabled by chronic pain for more than one year from a free intrapleural missile. Radiologic evidence of missile immobility and the tendency to observe chronically embedded missiles led to a delay in diagnosis. Intrapleural foreign bodies need to be considered in the evaluation of pain following chest or upper abdominal gunshot wounds."},
